# Flutter Security Rules

- Never hardcode secrets, private API keys, payment credentials, or admin credentials in the app.
- Store authentication tokens using the documented secure storage mechanism.
- Never log tokens, passwords, sensitive personal data, or payment data.
- Do not store unnecessary personal/location data locally.
- Enforce server authorization; client-side permission checks are UX only.
- Use secure transport (HTTPS/TLS) in non-development environments.
- Validate deep links/navigation inputs where external input can reach sensitive screens.
- Treat uploaded photos and proof-of-delivery media as sensitive operational data.
- Follow documented retention/deletion requirements and privacy UX.
